Third-party material
--------------------

Codexion (MIT), https://github.com/niu-io/codexion
  docs/EXTENSIONS.md — locator order, idempotent install/uninstall, versioned
  node ids, and fail-closed disable. The behavior is reimplemented here; no
  Codexion source files are copied.

Codex App HUD (MIT), https://github.com/sxy-kumako/codex-app-hud
  The active-thread probe `[data-app-action-sidebar-thread-id][aria-current="page"]`
  and the `local:<id>` sidebar form are used as documented in
  src/injector/README.md. Per-thread storage is keyed by the stable id, and
  draft `client-new-thread` ids are rejected. No HUD source files are copied.

Explodex, https://github.com/dan-dr/explodex
  No license is offered. Nothing from that repository is copied. Public
  architecture notes were used only as a list of sidebar attribute names
  (`data-app-action-sidebar-*`) and as a reminder that injected nodes need an
  explicit disposer list. Those names are recorded in codex-adapter/SELECTORS.md.
